  "findings": [
    {
      "subject": "Adapter delta",
      "result": "Source diff consists of a module wrapper; perf_fasta formal _n renamed n; top-level argument parsing moved into julia_main; entry resets the existing Int32 seed to 42 and returns Cint-compatible zero. Original generator, lookup, formatting, per-character writes, loop statements, constants, and probability arrays remain unchanged."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Lexical scope and boxing concern",
      "result": "perf_fasta has no nested function or closure, never reassigns n, and passes 2n/3n/5n directly to top-level repeat_fasta/random_fasta functions. Those functions contain no nested function or closure. The formal rename introduces no captured local apparent in source; no source evidence supports a Core.Box explanation. Original perf_fasta used a non-const global n despite accepting an unused _n formal."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Output path and concrete training signature",
      "result": "Both historical/current samplers direct child stdout to a regular temporary file. Training redirects stdout to mktemp IOStream. Pinned Base.init_stdio maps UV_FILE to fdio/IOStream. Retained trace explicitly requests precompile(Tuple{typeof(BenchFastaJulia3.perf_fasta), Int64, Base.IOStream}); a missing concrete IOStream training path is not supported by the trace."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Original per-byte IO cost",
      "result": "repeat_fasta/random_fasta write each sequence character individually in both sources. Base.write(::IOStream,::UInt8) checks writability and uses the stream lock around ios_putc in both cases. This identifies a shared expensive operation, not an adaptation difference or demonstrated cause of the measured regression."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Fresh state and amount of work",
      "result": "State starts at seed 42 in both processes. cumsum(pr) is nonmutating. All three current full outputs exactly match all retained JIT sample output hashes and byte counts: 254166745 bytes, SHA256 3fcf4f78104c8a65ef210fe1d469f4e473456c791225f2f1f9114f4986aa09fa."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Compiler metadata limit",
      "result": "PackageCompiler consumes traced concrete precompile statements and builds the image with -O3 --compile=all --strip-ir in the retained recipe. The trace records compilation requests, not optimized IR or machine-code performance. Static evidence does not identify a rejected specialization, boxed formal, changed stream class, extra output, or changed random-number kernel."
    }
  ],
